# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself.

# ── Supabase (frontend build only) ────────────────────────────────
# Vite bakes these into the bundle at BUILD time — they must be present
# wherever `npm run build` runs (including CI), not just on a server.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# There is no SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY entry here anymore.
# Every piece of server-side logic (create-user, update-user, delete-user,
# delete-timesheets, parse-timesheet, the reminder job) now runs as a
# Supabase Edge Function under supabase/functions/ — Supabase auto-injects
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY into every
# one of those at deploy time. Nothing in this repo runs server-side code
# locally against this .env file anymore; local dev is Vite-only
# (`npm run dev`), and Edge Functions are tested with `supabase functions
# serve` (which manages its own env), not this file.

# ── Microsoft Graph mail (daily timesheet reminders) ─────────────
# These four are read only by the Supabase Edge Functions, via
# `supabase secrets set`, never from this file:
#   supabase secrets set GRAPH_TENANT_ID=... GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=... \
#     GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=... GRAPH_SENDER_UPN=... APP_URL=https://yourdomain.com
#
# Entra app registration needs application permission Mail.Send (admin
# consent required), scoped to GRAPH_SENDER_UPN via an Exchange
# Application Access Policy — application Mail.Send otherwise grants
# send-as-anyone in the whole tenant.
#
# APP_URL is the deployed frontend's base URL (the VPS domain). Two uses:
# building the "Submit your timesheet" link in reminder emails, and (auth
# hardening Phase 4) locking every browser-facing Edge Function's CORS
# origin down to it instead of '*'. Supabase has no equivalent of
# Netlify's auto-injected site-URL env var since it doesn't host the
# frontend, so this has to be set explicitly once the domain exists.
#
# There is no REMINDER_TRIGGER_SECRET anymore — the function instead
# checks the Authorization header against SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, which
# Supabase auto-injects into every Edge Function and which the scheduling
# Cron job supplies explicitly (see migration_v14_schedule_reminders.sql),
# not guessed at.
#
# GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
# GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
# GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GRAPH_SENDER_UPN=
# APP_URL=
